In `replaceChangeCase`, `BytesRefs.toString(bc.right().fold())` can return `null` if the right-hand literal folds to a null value (e.g., `TO_UPPER(x) == null`). Passing `null` to `matchesCase` will throw a `NullPointerException` on `value.codePoints()`. Consider adding a null guard:
```java
var foldedRight = BytesRefs.toString(bc.right().fold());
if (foldedRight == null) {
    return bc; // leave unchanged; null comparisons are handled elsewhere
}
```
This prevents an optimizer crash on edge-case queries where a null literal appears on the right side of a comparison with a `ChangeCase` expression.

